    (
        4,
        2,
        "",
        "You shall not add to the word",
        "comm-contextual",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The “canonical formula.”</strong> The prohibition against adding to or subtracting from God’s commands appears here, again at 12:32, and is echoed in Proverbs 30:6 and Revelation 22:18–19. Ancient Near Eastern treaty texts contain similar “tamper clauses.” In later Jewish and Christian tradition this verse becomes the textual anchor for arguments about the closure of the canon. Within the Pentateuch itself, however, the principle is more about preserving covenant fidelity than fixing a list of books.",
        "User original",
    ),
