        "frontlets between your eyes",
        "comm",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>Tefillin and mezuzah.</strong> This verse, together with 6:8–9, is the textual basis for two enduring practices: <em>tefillin</em> (small leather boxes containing scripture passages, bound to head and arm during morning prayer) and <em>mezuzah</em> (a parchment scroll affixed to doorposts). Tefillin from the Second Temple period have been recovered at Qumran. The tradition reads the metaphor literally; some Christian and modern Jewish traditions read it figuratively. Both readings have ancient pedigrees.",
        "User original",
