    # ---- ch 28 ----
    (
        28,
        1,
        "",
        "set you high above all the nations",
        "comm-contextual",
        "Note",
        "Note",
        "<strong>The blessings.</strong> The blessings (28:1–14) are the shorter half of the covenant ratification. Note the rhetorical pattern: the chapter front-loads the blessings briefly and dwells extensively on the curses (vv. 15–68 — more than three times as long) — a classic ancient Near Eastern treaty pattern, designed to terrify the vassal into compliance. The book of Lamentations reads as a sustained meditation on the curses’ fulfillment.",
        "User original",
    ),
